From 8639058ca9bef04c7dbd3d43c50567cb0658a433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorenzo Giannoccaro <giannoccarol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:45:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Updater: time out stalled downloads and resume them by itself

A download whose network goes away while it runs blocked forever: the
connection had no read timeout, so read() never returned once a router
disconnected the device (band steering moves a phone between the 2.4 and
5 GHz access points) and Android reconnected it on a new network. The
app kept showing the same size, with no error, until the user paused and
resumed it.

Give the connection a 15 s connect timeout and a 30 s read timeout, so
such a download fails, and resume a failed download by itself after 10 s,
only on Wi-Fi or Ethernet, so that it never moves to mobile data without
the user. Up to 5 resumes in a row that get no data; data received resets
the count. Waiting for Wi-Fi or Ethernet does not count, for up to 10
minutes. A download the user pauses or deletes is left alone.

On a Lumia 930 with a router that disconnected it every 30-60 s, and an
Android that then kept its Wi-Fi off for 5 and 10 minutes, the download
went on by itself after each drop.

Change-Id: I55732dcc093de3c134e3a0d894fbf526599feb5a
